# Built from Forever's data: the Cenarion Circle quest rows (reputation from Forever's quest pages; the world
# database's standing gates: Aurel Goldleaf from Friendly, Abyssal Signets from Honored, Lords and Abyssal
# Scepters from Revered), the kill reputation and the standing each kill stops at (world database), the
# Encrypted Twilight Text drop table (about a third from every cultist, 87% from the Twilight Prophet), the
# spawns of the cultists and the Wind Stones, and the shops of Cenarion Hold with each item's standing and
# price from Forever's client item table. Neutral to Exalted is 42,000 reputation; druids start at Neutral
# 2,000 (the client's faction table). No race gets a reputation bonus in Forever; the Legacy perk Diplomat
# adds up to 10%. Numbers below are without it.
# INGAME: Do quests 6 or more levels below you still pay full reputation in Forever? In Classic they pay a
# fifth less per level past 5, down to a fifth; one beta report had a low quest paying in full.
# Forever changes: the Classic Silithus crafting patterns of Aendel Windspear (Dreamscale, Spitfire,
# Sandstalker, Bramblewood) and Vargus (Obsidian belts, Ironvine) are not in Forever's client; Forever adds 24
# patterns instead (Friendly and Honored, 7g 50s each). Forever's data names Mishta for the tailoring ones and
# Vargus for the blacksmithing ones, and no vendor for the leatherworking ones.
# Mortal Champions pays its 100 Cenarion reputation through a spell (client spell data), so Forever's quest
# page shows none.
# INGAME: Who sells Forever's new leatherworking patterns (Bileblister, Hivethrasher, Scalegut, Broodwatcher)?
# INGAME: Are the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj open? Blizzard's raid announcement for Forever names Barrow Deeps, Hyjal
# Summit and Onyxia's Lair; the Ruins are in the client but not announced.
# ASSUMED: Field Duty's captains and their silithid fight at the hives work as in Classic (Forever's data has
# the quests and the captains' spawns, no record of the fight). In-game check: does Captain Blackanvil (or
# Krug Skullsplit) sign the papers after the fight?

step The emissary in Ironforge
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Optional, and needed only for the Dredge quests later: Cenarion Emissary Jademoon sends you to Silithus with Taking Back Silithus, a 10-reputation letter. Skip it if you are already in Silithus.
  accept 8275 optional

step The emissary in Orgrimmar
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Optional, and needed only for the Dredge quests later: Cenarion Emissary Blackhoof sends you to Silithus with Taking Back Silithus, a 10-reputation letter. Skip it if you are already in Silithus.
  accept 8276 optional

step Cenarion Hold
  zone Silithus
  tip Cenarion Hold is the walled druid camp in north-central Silithus, with flight points for both sides. Everyone starts Neutral with the Cenarion Circle (druids at 2,000 of 3,000). Bor and Huum Wildmane stand together in the main building. Secret Communication opens the Encrypted Twilight Text turn-ins for good. The Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain; the numbers in this guide are without it.
  getfp "Cenarion Hold"
  turnin 8275 optional only Alliance  -- Windcaller Proudhorn
  turnin 8276 optional only Horde
  accept 8318                         -- Bor Wildmane
  accept 8320 optional                -- Huum Wildmane, level 60

step The cultist camp west of Cenarion Hold
  tip The nearest Twilight's Hammer camp lies just south-west of the Hold. Avengers, Geolords and Stonecallers (level 57 to 59) each drop an Encrypted Twilight Text about a third of the time, and every cultist kill is 1 reputation. Twilight Keeper Havunth walks the edge of the camp. Keep every cultist robe, cowl and mantle you loot: they are the Twilight Trappings for the Wind Stones later.
  collect 20404 x10 quest 8318.1      -- Encrypted Twilight Text
  kill 11881 x10 quest 8320.1 optional -- Twilight Geolord

step Back to Cenarion Hold
  turnin 8318
  turnin 8320 optional
  accept 8321 optional                -- Vyral the Vile

step Cultists until the top of Friendly, texts saved
  tip Neutral to Honored is 9,000 reputation (7,000 for druids). Every Twilight Avenger, Geolord, Stonecaller, Master and Overlord gives 1 reputation until 5,999 of 6,000 Friendly, one point short of Honored; there they stop. Save every Encrypted Twilight Text and leave the quests of the next steps for later: each kill below that point is a free point on top of its text, and the texts and quests pay the same at any standing. A text drops about every third kill, so 30 kills make 30 reputation and 10 texts (100 reputation later). Four camps: south-west of the Hold (39,44), the far west (26,34), the far south-west (19,84) and the north-east below Hive'Ashi (66,18: Overlords, and Flamereavers that count until the top of Honored). The Twilight Prophet (87% text) walks between 18,31 and 23,69. Texts sell on the auction house if you would rather buy. At 5,999 Friendly the last point into Honored comes from a Flamereaver, Twilight Keeper or Marauder, or from your first 10 texts at Bor Wildmane.
  note "Kills alone to the top of Friendly is 8,999 kills (6,999 for druids), but the texts they drop (about 3,000) are worth 30,000 more: most of the way to Exalted."
  note "Friendly (3,000) opens Kania's Formula: Enchant Cloak - Greater Fire Resistance (10g), Mishta's Cenarion Herb Bag (2g) and Sylvan Shoulders (5g), and Forever's new Friendly gloves patterns (7g 50s)."
  collect 20404 x10 nearest optional  -- Encrypted Twilight Text: save them
  kill 11880 optional                 -- Twilight Avenger
  kill 11882 optional                 -- Twilight Stonecaller
  kill 15213 optional                 -- Twilight Overlord
  kill 15201 optional @69.8,14.3      -- Twilight Flamereaver: still counts at 5,999 Friendly
  turnin 8319 direct optional         -- Bor Wildmane: 10 texts, 100, for the last point
  rep 609 Honored

step Vyral the Vile
  tip Vyral the Vile (level 61, not elite) waits at the back of Twilight's Run, the cave in the north-east of Silithus. Flamereavers and Twilight Masters guard the way: the Flamereavers count until the top of Honored, the Masters stop at the top of Friendly like the other cultists.
  collect 20466 quest 8321.1 optional @72.4,15.6 -- Vyral's Signet Ring
  turnin 8321 optional

step Silithus quests at Cenarion Hold
  tip Now cash in the one-time quests: about 1,700 reputation alone, 2,400 with the group quests. They are level 55 to 60, so they pay in full at 60. Securing the Supply Lines needs Taking Back Silithus first. Deathclasp is an elite scorpid with two guards (group of 2 or 3). Calandrath's Desert Recipe is for Cooks: its recipe makes the Smoked Desert Dumplings he wants.
  accept 8277                         -- Beetix Ficklespragg
  accept 8280 optional                -- Windcaller Proudhorn, after Taking Back Silithus
  accept 8284                         -- Geologist Larksbane
  accept 8304                         -- Commander Mar'alith
  accept 8283 optional                -- Wanted poster: Deathclasp, elite
  accept 8307 optional                -- Calandrath, for Cooks
  accept 9415 optional only Alliance  -- Rifleman Torrig: Report to Marshal Bluewall
  accept 9416 optional only Horde     -- Scout Bloodfist: Report to General Kirika

step Around Cenarion Hold
  tip Stonelash Scorpids and Sand Skitterers roam the sands around the Hold; Dredge Strikers dig north-east of it. The Sandy Cookbook lies in the cultist camp south-west of the Hold.
