step Quests elsewhere
  tip The Cenarion Circle's other quests are spread over Kalimdor and the Plaguelands. In Classic a quest pays less once it is 6 or more levels below you (a fifth less per level, down to a fifth): at 60, The Wildlife Suffers Too (Mulgris Deepriver, Western Plaguelands, levels 54 and 56) would pay 60 and 75 instead of 75 and 75, and Corruption of Earth and Seed (Maraudon, level 51) 30 instead of 150. Your first turn-in shows which rule Forever uses. Shards of the Felvine (Rabine Saturna, level 60, the Felvine Shard from Alzzin in Dire Maul) pays 150 and its Reliquary 100 at any level.
  note Do the Western Plaguelands and Maraudon quests while you level; at 60 they may pay a fraction.

step Encrypted Twilight Texts to Revered
  zone Silithus
  tip Honored to Revered is 12,000 reputation. Bor Wildmane takes 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts for 100 reputation, again and again, until Exalted: 120 turn-ins (1,200 texts) to Revered without the quests, or about 950 texts after them. Hand in the texts you saved now. The cultists no longer count, but the Flamereavers, Twilight Keepers, Marauders and Templars count until 11,999 of 12,000 Honored, and the Twilight Lord Everun and Prophet until Exalted. Honored opens Kania's Formula: Enchant Cloak - Greater Nature Resistance (10g), Mishta's Pattern: Sylvan Crown (5g) and Forever's new Honored patterns (7g 50s each).
  collect 20404 x10 nearest optional  -- Encrypted Twilight Text
  turnin 8319 direct optional         -- Bor Wildmane: 10 texts, 100
  rep 609 Revered

step Field Duty, level 60
  tip Windcaller Kaldon stands by the moonwell of Cenarion Hold. Field Duty (25 reputation, repeatable) sends you with unsigned papers to your side's captain: Captain Blackanvil's Ironforge Brigade outside Hive'Zora (Alliance) or Krug Skullsplit's Orgrimmar Legion outside Hive'Regal (Horde). Use the papers first, then talk to the captain: a level 60 elite silithid attacks; keep the captain alive and he signs. Kaldon then lets you pick a Combat, Logistics or Tactical Assignment, each holding a random briefing worth 50 reputation and a badge: 30 hive silithid kills (elites), goods such as 30 Heavy Runecloth Bandages or 3 Ornate Mithril Boots, or one Templar, Twilight Marauder or scout report. One badge of each kind buys Allegiance to Cenarion Circle at Kaldon: 200 reputation, repeatable. A full round is about 375 reputation.
  accept 8507 optional only Alliance  -- Windcaller Kaldon
  accept 8731 optional only Horde
  collect 20810 quest 8507.1 optional only Alliance @32.8,52.6 -- Signed Field Duty Papers, Captain Blackanvil
  collect 20810 quest 8731.1 optional only Horde @51.4,68.4 -- Signed Field Duty Papers, Krug Skullsplit
  turnin 8507 optional only Alliance
  turnin 8731 optional only Horde
  turnin 9338 direct optional         -- Allegiance: one Combat, Logistics and Tactical badge, 200
  accept 8800 optional                -- Cenarion Battlegear: Vargus's badge gear
  turnin 8800 optional

step Silithyst
  tip Optional, 100 reputation once: Scouring the Desert. Your side's camp sits by a hive: Marshal Bluewall's by Hive'Zora (Alliance), General Kirika's by Hive'Regal (Horde). Silithyst rises from glowing geysers around the desert: walk through one, carry the Silithyst to your camp's Silithyst Extractor, then talk to the camp's leader. It is a world PvP objective: players of the other side can take it from you.
  turnin 9415 optional only Alliance @33.3,51.1 -- Marshal Bluewall
  accept 9419 optional only Alliance
  complete 9419 optional only Alliance @33.0,50.8 -- deliver Silithyst at the extractor
  turnin 9419 optional only Alliance  -- 100
  turnin 9416 optional only Horde @50.8,69.5 -- General Kirika
  accept 9422 optional only Horde
  complete 9422 optional only Horde @50.9,69.3 -- deliver Silithyst at the extractor
  turnin 9422 optional only Horde     -- 100

step Templars and the Abyssal Council
  tip Wearing a full set of Twilight Trappings (cultist Cowl, Mantle and Robe, about 8%, 8% and 6% per cultist) lets you use a Lesser Wind Stone: two stand in each of the three western camps. A random Abyssal Templar appears: a level 60 elite for 1 to 3 players, 5 reputation until the top of Honored and an Abyssal Crest 93% of the time. The summon uses up the set (and later the medallion and ring too), and if the elemental gets away they are gone: summon only when you can win. Abyssal Contacts pays 100 for the first crest; after that Bor takes 3 crests for 50. From Friendly, Huum Wildmane sends you to Aurel Goldleaf: 3 crests and a Large Brilliant Shard buy the Medallion of Station that, worn with a set, opens the larger Wind Stone for a Duke (level 62 elite, group of 5; 25 reputation, Abyssal Signet 85%).
  accept 8361 optional                -- Bor Wildmane
  collect 20513 quest 8361.1 optional @24.4,36.0 -- Abyssal Crest: Templar, group of 1 to 3
  turnin 8361 optional
  turnin 8362 direct optional         -- 3 Abyssal Crests: 50
  accept 8331 optional                -- Huum Wildmane, Friendly
  turnin 8331 optional                -- Aurel Goldleaf
  accept 8332 optional
  turnin 8332 optional                -- 3 crests and a Large Brilliant Shard: the Medallion of Station
  accept 8349 optional
  turnin 8349 optional                -- Bor Wildmane
  accept 8348 optional
  collect 20514 quest 8348.1 optional @24.7,32.7 -- Abyssal Signet: Duke, group of 5
  turnin 8348 optional

step Signets and scepters to Exalted
  tip Revered to Exalted is 21,000 reputation: 210 text turn-ins (2,100 texts), or less with the rest. From Honored, Bor takes 3 Abyssal Signets for 100 (each Duke also gives 25, to Exalted), and Aurel takes one Abyssal Scepter for A Humble Offering (200, once). From Revered, Goldleaf's Discovery leads to Lords of the Council: 3 signets and 5 Large Brilliant Shards buy the Ring of Lordship, and set, medallion and ring open the Greater Wind Stone for an Abyssal Lord: a level 63 boss for a raid of about 20, 50 reputation, and an Abyssal Scepter. Bor pays 200 for the first scepter and 150 for each 3 after. Revered opens Mishta's Satchel of Cenarius (5g), Gaea's Embrace (9g) and Sylvan Vest (5g); Exalted is the standing for Champion's Battlegear at Vargus.
